{
  "character": "働",
  "summary": {
    "text": "働 is a Japanese-created character meaning “work,” read hataraku in Japanese. Its visible parts suggest a person, 亻, and movement, 動. That association offers a useful way to remember it, but these sources do not document how or when the character was first devised.",
    "evidence_ids": [
      "E4",
      "E5",
      "E10",
      "E24"
    ]
  },
  "history": [
    {
      "text": "The Chinese-language note concerns a later borrowing of the written Japanese character. It gives a Chinese pronunciation based on 動. That explains the Chinese reading in this record; it does not explain the original Japanese choice of components.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "E1"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    {
      "text": "The available material identifies 働 as a kokuji, a character created in Japan, but supplies no early Japanese attestations or account of its coinage. The component-based memory aid therefore remains separate from a documented origin story.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "E4",
        "E6"
      ]
    }
  ],
